      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5e8c2e14af4a860606a60ca3|full_name}: not necessarily, because the end of the shoulder is attached to the upper arm where the tracker should be thus giving us info on the position of the shoulder joint. As long as the elbow tracker is mounted on the upper arm and not the lower arm, shoulder tracking without a chest tracker is possible in theory.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
